# Scope

This rule applies **only** to this project: the local Feeding App workspace and GitHub repo `hemvanh/feeding-app`. Do not use these branch roles or the **publish all** phrase in any other repo.

# Branch roles

This repo has two jobs. Do not mix them.

- **`main`**: live GitHub Pages site only. Root is the built `dist` files (`index.html`, `feeding-data.json`, icons). Do not merge source (`src/`, `package.json`, etc.) into `main`.
- **`dev`**: active development with AI. Source of truth for the Vite app. Work, commits, and PRs happen here.

When publishing: `npm run build` on `dev`, then copy `dist` contents onto `main` and commit there. Do not merge `dev` → `main`.

Stay on `dev` unless the user explicitly asks to update the live Pages files on `main`.

# Phrase: "publish all"

When the user says **publish all**, do this in order without asking again:

1. On **`dev`**: stage only the relevant source changes, commit, and `git push origin dev`.
2. On **`dev`**: run `npm run build`.
3. Copy built `dist` files onto **`main`** (`index.html`, `favicon.svg`, `icons.svg`). Do **not** overwrite live `feeding-data.json` unless the user asks. Do **not** commit `dist/` or `node_modules/` onto `main`. Do **not** merge `dev` into `main`.
4. Commit and `git push origin main`.
5. Check out **`dev`** again and leave that as the active branch.

Skip an empty `dev` commit if there is nothing to commit; still build and update `main` if the live site needs the latest build.
